        "original_id": "f7a3e55a-fec8-52b9-8ee8-9104a63646ae",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: One Liberty Plaza, 1717 Broadway, Barclay Tower, Lower Manhattan, Manhattan, Tribeca, New York City, United States\n- Organizations: Cleary Gottlieb Steen & Hamilton LLP\n- Buildings: U.S. Steel Building, Singer Building, City Investing Building\n\nFacts:\n- One Liberty Plaza, formerly the U.S. Steel Building, is a skyscraper in Lower Manhattan in New York City.\n- One Liberty Plaza stands at the site of the former Singer Building and the former City Investing Building in Lower Manhattan.\n- The Singer Building was the tallest structure ever dismantled.\n- Cleary Gottlieb Steen & Hamilton LLP is an international law firm headquartered at One Liberty Plaza in New York City.\n- Barclay Tower is a skyscraper in the Tribeca neighborhood of Lower Manhattan in New York City.\n- 1717 Broadway is a skyscraper in Manhattan, New York City, United States.\n- 1717 Broadway is 750 feet tall and is the tallest hotel in North America.",
